{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And the land shall not vomit you out</b> — that is, it is not enough for you that retribution is paid through vomiting alone, but rather what does it mean, ״for whoever does any of these abominations״ — ״those persons shall be cut off.״" "<b>As it vomited out.</b> We find masculine language for a feminine noun — ולא נשא אותם הארץ, נעתם ארץ ישוב אל הארץ. And one may say that the expression lacks the word היא, as if written כאשר קאה היא את הגוי, like ורחל באה עם הצאן."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {1 "The phrase ולא נשא אותם הארץ, נעתם ארץ ישוב אל הארץ is textually obscure; translated hyper-literally as it stands. It may be corrupt or elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:20.070014749Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}